      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Hanging for a second during a loop like that, especially when dealing with Excel, is often due to Excel having to refresh or recalculate things behind the scenes. You can make the code run much smoother and faster by temporarily turning off screen updating and automatic calculation.\n\nBefore your loop starts, add `Application.ScreenUpdating = False` and `Application.Calculation = xlCalculationManual`. Then, make sure to set them back to `True` and `xlCalculationAutomatic` right before the `End Sub`. This prevents Excel from drawing every single change as it happens, which is a huge performance drain.\n\nHere is how your sub should look now, incorporating these optimizations. It should run almost instantaneously, even with 500 iterations.\n\n```vba\nSub MonthlyRecon()\n    Dim wsRecon As Worksheet\n    Dim i As Integer\n    Set wsRecon = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(\"Recon_Data_Final\")\n    \n    ' Optimization Block: Stop Excel from drawing and recalculating while the code runs\n    Application.ScreenUpdating = False\n    Application.Calculation = xlCalculationManual\n    \n    For i = 2 To 500\n        wsRecon.Cells",
